<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Experience (XP)</h1>
<p>Experience is usually gained by killing monsters, and by solving quests. The 
experience you gain from a kill depends on the monster's level compared to 
yours: more for a monster above you, less for one below, and none at all for 
one seven or more levels below you. In a group, or when someone of a higher 
level has also fought the monster, it is compared with the highest level 
among them.
</p><p>You gain no experience when killing players.
</p><p>If you are good and kill evil you get a bonus. Vice versa, but not quite as 
large.
</p><p>In a group, everyone in the group who is in the room when the monster dies 
gets a share (see <a cmd='#'>Help Groups</a>); a member more than five levels below the 
highest gets less. 
When you die, you lose some experience (see <a cmd='#'>Help Die</a>). With enough experience 
you can raise a level (see <a cmd='#'>Help Level</a>).
</p><p><br />
See Also:
